":"Yes, hot meals are available.","D":"The lights are bright."},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (B): \"Yes, hot meals are available.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list1_m2_q7","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"Is dinner available here? Can I bring food from outside I bring food from outside I bring food from outside ?","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"I like sandwiches.","A":"No, only cafeteria meals.","B":"Yes, the food is hot.","D":"It''s in the library."},"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (A): \"No, only cafeteria meals.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list1_m2_q8","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"? Where is the register? Where is the register?","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"It''s very interesting.","A":"At the front of the cafeteria.","B":"I''m going to class.","D":"Yes, I read it."},"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (A): \"At the front of the cafeteria.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."}]}},{"id":"list1_m2_t2","title":"Task 2: Campus Conversation","task_type":"conversation","content":{"context_title":"Hội thoại tình huống sinh viên","audio_text":"Where is the register? Listen to a conversation. Did you Listen to a conversation. Did you Listen to a conversation. Did you return the library book? return the library book? return the library book? Yes, but it Yes, but it was delayed by 2 days. was delayed by 2 days. was delayed by 2 days. I had to pay a fine I had to pay a fine I had to pay a fine . That is very That is very That is very sad. Is it sad. Is it sad. Is it expensive? Just expensive? Just expensive? Just a few a few a few dollars, but dollars, but dollars, but they add up they add up they add up . I''ll set a reminder next time I''ll set a reminder next time I''ll set a reminder next time . Listen to . Listen to","questions":[{"id":"list1_m2_q9","prompt":"Why did the man have to pay money?","options":{"A":"He lost a book.","B":"He damaged a book.","C":"He returned a book late.","D":"He borrowed too many books."},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án (C) chính xác: \"He returned a book late.\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."},{"id":"list1_m2_q10","prompt":"IA .r What does the man plan to do in the future?","options":{"A":"Avoid borrowing books","B":"Use a reminder to return books on time","C":"Ask the woman to return books for him","D":"Renew his books online"},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (B): \"Use a reminder to return books on time\". Dựa vào chi tiết trực tiếp được người nói đề cập trong bài nghe."}]}},{"id":"list1_m2_t3","title":"Task 3: Campus Announcement","task_type":"announcement","content":{"context_title":"Thông báo hành chính đại học","audio_text":". Listen to the announcement in the campus library. the announcement in the campus library. the announcement in the campus library. Good morning. Due to upgrades to our Good morning. Due to upgrades to our Good morning. Due to upgrades to our computer system , the , the , the online catalog will be unavailable catalog will be unavailable from 6pm tonight until noon tomorrow from 6pm tonight until noon tomorrow from 6pm tonight until noon tomorrow . At this time . At this time , you , you , you cannot renew or hold books online. Please cannot renew or hold books online. Please complete any urgent transactions by 6pm complete any urgent transactions by 6pm complete any urgent transactions by 6pm . Sorry for the inconvenience, Sorry for the inconvenience, Sorry for the inconvenience, thank you for your patience. thank you for your patience. Listen to","questions":[{"id":"list1_m2_q11","prompt":"What is the main purpose of the announcement?","options":{"A":"To announce new library services","B":"To explain a temporary system outage","C":"To invite students to a training session","D":"To advertise online resources"},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án chính xác là (B): \"To explain a temporary system outage\". Thông tin trọng tâm xuyên suốt bài nghe nhấn mạnh vào ý chính này."},{"id":"list1_m2_q12","prompt":"What should students do if they need to renew a book today?","options":{"A":"Wait until tomorrow morning","B":"Renew it before 6 P.M.","C":"Ask a librarian to waive fees","D":"Call the IT department"},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (B): \"Renew it before 6 P.M.\". Dựa vào chi tiết trực tiếp được người nói đề cập trong bài nghe."}]}},{"id":"list1_m2_t4","title":"Task 4: Academic Lecture","task_type":"academic_talk","content":{"context_title":"Bài giảng học thuật chuyên sâu","audio_text":"Listen to Listen to Listen to the lecture in biology class. the lecture in biology class. the lecture in biology class. Photosynthesis is the process by which plants is the process by which plants convert light energy into chemical energy convert light energy into chemical energy convert light energy into chemical energy . Most people Most people Most people know that plants absorb carbon dioxide and release oxygen. But what is know that plants absorb carbon dioxide and release oxygen. But what is know that plants absorb carbon dioxide and release oxygen. But what is less discussed is that discussed is that photosynthesis occurs in two main stages. occurs in two main stages. occurs in two main stages. Actions that depend on light and Actions that depend on light and Actions that depend on light and actions that do not depend on light. actions that do not depend on light. actions that do not depend on light. Light- dependent processes occur in chloroplasts, occur in chloroplasts, occur in chloroplasts, where sunlight is sunlight is sunlight is absorbed by chlorophyll and absorbed by chlorophyll and converted into two forms of energy, ATP and NADPH. converted into two forms of energy, ATP and NADPH. converted into two forms of energy, ATP and NADPH. The processes that do not depend on light are The processes that do not depend on light are The processes that do not depend on light are often called the Calvin cycle, called the Calvin cycle, called the Calvin cycle, which uses that energy to which uses that energy to which uses that energy to convert carbon dioxide into glucose. This convert carbon dioxide into glucose. This convert carbon dioxide into glucose. This two-stage system is very system is very system is very efficient . Without it, . Without it, . Without it, plants would plants would not be able to store energy and the not be able to store energy and the not be able to store energy and the food chains that depend on them, chains that depend on them, chains that depend on them, ultimately including humans, including humans, including humans, would collapse would collapse . Oops.","questions":[{"id":"list1_m2_q13","prompt":"What is the main focus of the talk?","options":{"A":"How sunlight is formed","B":"The two stages of photosynthesis","C":"Why humans breathe oxygen","D":"The role of chloroplasts in animals"},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án chính xác là (B): \"The two stages of photosynthesis\". Thông tin trọng tâm xuyên suốt bài nghe nhấn mạnh vào ý chính này."},{"id":"list1_m2_q14","prompt":"What does the professor say about ATP and NADPH?","options":{"A":"They are created during the Calvin cycle.","B":"They store light energy for later use.","C":"They are waste products of respiration.","D":"They break down glucose molecules."},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (B): \"They store light energy for later use.\". Dựa vào chi tiết trực tiếp được người nói đề cập trong bài nghe."},{"id":"list1_m2_q15","prompt":"What does the speaker imply about food chains?","options":{"A":"They would not exist without photosynthesis.","B":"They are independent of plant life.","C":"They rely primarily on animal respiration.","D":"They are maintained by oxygen alone."},"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (A): \"They would not exist without photosynthesis.\". Đây là suy luận hợp lý nhất từ các chi tiết ngầm định của người nói."},{"id":"list1_m2_q16","prompt":"Why does the professor call the system \"efficient\"?","options":{"A":"It creates both oxygen and nitrogen.","B":"It stores energy in a usable form.","C":"It prevents plants from overheating.","D":"It produces more glucose than needed."},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án (B) chính xác: \"It stores energy in a usable form.\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."}]}}]}],"description":"Bộ đề TOEFL iBT Listening 2026 chuẩn ETS. Chủ đề trọng tâm: Cafeteria, Medical Clinic, Library System, Silk Road, Photosynthesis. Gồm Module 1 (14.5 phút) và Module 2 (14.5 phút - Adaptive) với đầy đủ phản xạ hội thoại, thông báo và bài giảng học thuật.","youtube_url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PVfKsFWhgOE","source":"YouTube TOEFL 2026 Listening Practice 1","created_at_ms":1791231607965}'::jsonb,
