  '{"stages":[{"id":"list10_stage_1","title":"Listening - Module 1 (Stage 1)","duration_seconds":870,"description":"Module 1 gồm các dạng bài: Choose a Response, Conversation, Announcement, Academic Talk. Hoàn thành trong 14.5 phút.","tasks":[{"id":"list10_m1_t1","title":"Task 1: Listen & Choose a Response (8 câu)","task_type":"choose_response","content":{"instructions":"Lắng nghe câu nói ngắn và chọn phản xạ trả lời phù hợp nhất theo chuẩn giao tiếp đại học Bắc Mỹ.","questions":[{"id":"list10_m1_q1","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"module 1 I didn''t understand the grading policy","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"Grades are important.","A":"It''s explained in the syllabus.","B":"I got a good grade.","D":"Don''t worry, it will arrive soon."},"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (A): \"It''s explained in the syllabus.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list10_m1_q2","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"the classroom projector isn''t working","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"Projectors are expensive.","A":"I brought my laptop.","B":"That''s because the room is dark.","D":"Let''s tell the instructor."},"correct_answer":"D","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (D): \"Let''s tell the instructor.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list10_m1_q3","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"how early should we arrive for the interview","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"At least 15 minutes early.","A":"I arrived late.","B":"The interview is hard.","D":"Interviews are stressful."},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (C): \"At least 15 minutes early.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list10_m1_q4","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"I''m unsure how to format the paper","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"I typed mine.","A":"The paper is long.","B":"It''s in the paper tray.","D":"Follow the style guide."},"correct_answer":"D","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (D): \"Follow the style guide.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list10_m1_q5","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"did you sign up for the workshop","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"You didn''t need to sign the document.","A":"I enjoy them very much.","B":"It will be canceled.","D":"Yes, I registered yesterday."},"correct_answer":"D","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (D): \"Yes, I registered yesterday.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list10_m1_q6","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"the professor hasn''t replied yet","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"Maybe wait another day.","A":"Replies should be written in","B":"I sent an email.","D":"What did you do?"},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (C): \"Maybe wait another day.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list10_m1_q7","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"is there a deadline to add classes","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"Yes, by the end of this week.","A":"I added one.","B":"No, it''s free.","D":"Classes are full."},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (C): \"Yes, by the end of this week.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list10_m1_q8","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"discussion section was canceled","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"Not necessarily.","A":"Discussions are helpful.","B":"Thanks for telling me.","D":"It was loud."},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (B): \"Thanks for telling me.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."}]}},{"id":"list10_m1_t2","title":"Task 2: Campus Conversation 1","task_type":"conversation","content":{"context_title":"Hội thoại sinh viên 1","audio_text":"did you buy a gift for Emma''s birthday yet not yet I''ve been thinking about it all week but I still can''t make up my mind I had a few ideas but none of them felt right I want to get her something special I''m not sure what kind of books she likes these days that makes sense then maybe play it safe and get her a gift card for the bookstore that way she can choose what she wants that''s actually a great idea it''s simple but still thoughtful and it saves but still thoughtful and it saves you from stressing over the choice true thanks I think I finally made up my mind","questions":[{"id":"list10_m1_q9","prompt":"Why hasn''t the man bought a gift yet?","options":{"A":"He forgot about the birthday","B":"He was too busy shopping","C":"He couldn''t decide what to buy","D":"He doesn''t know what Emma likes"},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án (C) chính xác: \"He couldn''t decide what to buy\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."},{"id":"list10_m1_q10","prompt":"What does the woman suggest?","options":{"A":"Buying a novel","B":"Asking Emma directly","C":"Ordering online","D":"Getting a bookstore gift card"},"correct_answer":"D","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (D): \"Getting a bookstore gift card\". Đây là suy luận hợp lý nhất từ các chi tiết ngầm định của người nói."}]}},{"id":"list10_m1_t3","title":"Task 3: Campus Conversation 2","task_type":"conversation","content":{"context_title":"Hội thoại sinh viên 2","audio_text":"I can''t find my student ID card anywhere and I''m starting to panic are you sure did you check your backpack and all your pockets yeah I checked everything twice it''s nowhere to be found when was the last time you used it this morning I think I used it to enter the library before class I hope so but I needed to enter the dorm and borrow books I can''t really wait then you should go to the student services office and request a replacement do they charge for that yes but only a small fee that''s good I was worried it would be expensive I was worried it would be expensive the better you''re right I''ll head there after class","questions":[{"id":"list10_m1_q11","prompt":"Why is the man worried about the situation?","options":{"A":"He needs the card for several daily activities","B":"His exam is stored on the card","C":"The card contains money","D":"His professor needs to see the card"},"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Đáp án (A) chính xác: \"He needs the card for several daily activities\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."},{"id":"list10_m1_q12","prompt":"What does the woman say about getting a replacement?","options":{"A":"It is free","B":"It requires an appointment","C":"It involves a small charge","D":"It takes a few days"},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (C): \"It involves a small charge\". Dựa vào chi tiết trực tiếp được người nói đề cập trong bài nghe."}]}},{"id":"list10_m1_t4","title":"Task 4: Campus Announcement 1","task_type":"announcement","content":{"context_title":"Thông báo khuôn viên trường 1","audio_text":"listen to an announcement during a campus tour as we approach The West Wing of the science building Please be aware that this section is under renovation access to the main Laboratories will be restricted until mid-april classes scheduled in these Labs have been temporarily moved to the north Wing maps with updated classroom locations with updated classroom locations are available at the information desk","questions":[{"id":"list10_m1_q13","prompt":"What is the main topic of the announcement?","options":{"A":"A change in classroom locations","B":"A new laboratory opening","C":"A special science lecture","D":"A new building construction project"},"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Đáp án chính xác là (A): \"A change in classroom locations\". Thông tin trọng tâm xuyên suốt bài nghe nhấn mạnh vào ý chính này."},{"id":"list10_m1_q14","prompt":"Why does the announcer mention the information desk?","options":{"A":"TO tell students where to borrow equipment","B":"TO show where they can find updated maps","C":"TO explain where to register for lab classes","D":"TO encourage students to ask questions"},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án (B) chính xác: \"TO show where they can find updated maps\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."}]}},{"id":"list10_m1_t5","title":"Task 5: Campus Announcement 2","task_type":"announcement","content":{"context_title":"Thông báo khuôn viên trường 2","audio_text":"listen to an announcement in a supermarket attention shoppers due to a temporary issue with our payment system card transactions at self-checkout stations are currently unavailable please proceed to register 3 through 8 for assisted checkout our technical team is working to resolve the issue as is working to resolve the issue as quickly as possible we apologize for the inconvenience and appreciate your patience","questions":[{"id":"list10_m1_q15","prompt":"What is the main topic of the announcement?","options":{"A":"A store closing early","B":"A payment system issue","C":"A discount on groceries","D":"A new checkout system"},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án chính xác là (B): \"A payment system issue\". Thông tin trọng tâm xuyên suốt bài nghe nhấn mạnh vào ý chính này."},{"id":"list10_m1_q16","prompt":"Why are customers asked to go to registers 3 through 8?","options":{"A":"To pay with cash only","B":"TO return damaged products","C":"To complete purchases with staff assistance","D":"TO receive coupons"},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án (C) chính xác: \"To complete purchases with staff assistance\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."}]}},{"id":"list10_m1_t6","title":"Task 6: Academic Lecture","task_type":"academic_talk","content":{"context_title":"Bài giảng học thuật đại học","audio_text":"listen to part of a Linguistics class around the world thousands of languages are spoken today yet many are at risk of Disappearing linguists estimate that a large percentage of the languages currently spoken may vanish within the next Century this often happens when younger Generations stop what happens when younger generation stop learning their communities native language and instead adopt a more widely spoken one language loss effects more than communication languages often contain unique ways of understanding the world including cultural knowledge oral history and traditional practices traditional practices when a language disappears communities may lose important parts of their identity to address this issue language preservation programs have expanded some communities record Elders speaking the language so future Generations can study pronunciation and vocabulary educational apps and school programs designed to encourage children to use the language in daily life still preservation efforts face challenges Reviving a language requires long-term Commitment Community involvement Community involvement and sufficient resources some experts argue that documentation alone is not enough a language truly survives only if people actively use it in everyday communication as technology improves preservation may become easier however the however the future of endangered languages will depend largely on whether younger Generations choose to keep them alive","questions":[{"id":"list10_m1_q17","prompt":"What is the talk mainly about?","options":{"A":"How children naturally learn multiple languages","B":"The causes of language loss and preservation efforts","C":"The importance of dictionaries in language learning","D":"The history of writing systems across cultures"},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án chính xác là (B): \"The causes of language loss and preservation efforts\". Thông tin trọng tâm xuyên suốt bài nghe nhấn mạnh vào ý chính này."},{"id":"list10_m1_q18","prompt":"Why is language loss considered significant?","options":{"A":"It makes translation more expensive","B":"It reduces the number of available books","C":"Cultural knowledge and traditions may disappear","D":"It simplifies grammar over time"},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án (C) chính xác: \"Cultural knowledge and traditions may disappear\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."},{"id":"list10_m1_q19","prompt":"Why does the speaker mention educational apps?","options":{"A":"To criticize society''s dependence on technology","B":"To give an example of a preservation strategy","C":"To compare traditional and modern learning","D":"To discuss preparation for language exams"},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án (B) chính xác: \"To give an example of a preservation strategy\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."},{"id":"list10_m1_q20","prompt":"What does the speaker imply about language preservation?","options":{"A":"Documentation alone may not keep a language alive","B":"Most endangered languages will survive with technology","C":"Schools often oppose preservation efforts","D":"Technology guarantees successful preservation"},"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (A): \"Documentation alone may not keep a language alive\". Đây là suy luận hợp lý nhất từ các chi tiết ngầm định của người nói."}]}}]},{"id":"list10_stage_2","title":"Listening - Module 2 (Stage 2 - HARD)","duration_seconds":870,"description":"Module 2 cấp độ nâng cao (Hard): kiểm tra khả năng suy luận, nắm bắt ý chính và chi tiết học thuật.","tasks":[{"id":"list10_m2_t1","title":"Task 1: Listen & Choose a Response (8 câu)","task_type":"choose_response","content":{"instructions":"Lắng nghe câu nói ngắn và chọn phản xạ trả lời phù hợp nhất theo chuẩn giao tiếp đại học Bắc Mỹ.","questions":[{"id":"list10_m2_q1","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"module 2 can I retake the quiz","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"Quizzes are short.","A":"Retakes don''t help.","B":"I''m in the same boat.","D":"You should ask the instructor."},"correct_answer":"D","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (D): \"You should ask the instructor.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list10_m2_q2","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"where can I get tutoring for math","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"I need to hit the books too.","A":"At the learning center.","B":"Yes, of course.","D":"Math is hard."},"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (A): \"At the learning center.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list10_m2_q3","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"did you save me a seat","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"Yes, it''s right here.","A":"The lecture is full.","B":"No big deal.","D":"Seats are limited."},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (C): \"Yes, it''s right here.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list10_m2_q4","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"I''m struggling with this research paper","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"Hang in there - you''re almost done.","A":"I finished mine yesterday.","B":"Research is important.","D":"Papers are long."},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (C): \"Hang in there - you''re almost done.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list10_m2_q5","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"I''m not sure I can solve this problem","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"Give it a shot first.","A":"The answer is wrong.","B":"Problems take time.","D":"I solved it already."},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (C): \"Give it a shot first.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list10_m2_q6","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"I don''t understand this feedback","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"I''m sure it''s clear.","A":"I got feedback too.","B":"Let''s read it together.","D":"I don''t see it this way."},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (B): \"Let''s read it together.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list10_m2_q7","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"I forgot to save my work and my computer crashed","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"I bought mine online.","A":"That sounds frustrating. Back to the drawing","B":"Computers are expensive.","D":"The screen is very bright."},"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (A): \"That sounds frustrating. Back to the drawing\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list10_m2_q8","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"are late submissions accepted","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"I turned mine in early.","A":"Otherwise, you''re out of luck.","B":"You should submit your work online.","D":"Only with a valid reason."},"correct_answer":"D","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (D): \"Only with a valid reason.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."}]}},{"id":"list10_m2_t2","title":"Task 2: Campus Conversation","task_type":"conversation","content":{"context_title":"Hội thoại sinh viên (Phần nâng cao)","audio_text":"did you hand in your history paper yet I just submitted mine a few minutes ago not yet I''m planning to go over mine One Last Time seriously I thought you finished it yesterday I did more or less but I''m still not fully satisfied with some of my arguments a few paragraphs feel slightly repetitive honestly I doubt the professor will notice minor wording issues your papers are always strong maybe but I know myself the deadline is this afternoon at 3:00 isn''t it yes I have isn''t it yes I have plenty of time I''ll submit it right after my biology class you really do double-check everything I wish I were that discipline exactly better safe than sorry that''s hard to argue with maybe I should start doing the same","questions":[{"id":"list10_m2_q9","prompt":"What does the man imply about the woman?","options":{"A":"She often submits work late","B":"She is very careful with her work","C":"She struggles with writing papers","D":"She depends heavily on others"},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (B): \"She is very careful with her work\". Đây là suy luận hợp lý nhất từ các chi tiết ngầm định của người nói."},{"id":"list10_m2_q10","prompt":"What does the woman mean by \"Better safe than sorry\"?","options":{"A":"Working quickly saves time","B":"Feeling sorry helps people improve","C":"Deadlines should be flexible for better results","D":"Taking extra precautions is wiser than risking"},"correct_answer":"D","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (D): \"Taking extra precautions is wiser than risking\". Dựa vào chi tiết trực tiếp được người nói đề cập trong bài nghe."}]}},{"id":"list10_m2_t3","title":"Task 3: Campus Announcement","task_type":"announcement","content":{"context_title":"Thông báo khuôn viên trường (Phần nâng cao)","audio_text":"listen to an announcement in a medical clinic good afternoon patience due to an unexpected Staffing shortage we are currently operating with reduced capacity as a result wait times are significantly longer than usual and patience with scheduled appointments should expect delays of approximately is it expect delays of approximately 30 to 45 minutes please be assured that all appointments will still be honored today however if this delay creates a scheduling conflict we encourage you to speak with reception to discuss alternative appointment times we sincerely apologize for the inconvenience and appreciate your patience appreciate your patience","questions":[{"id":"list10_m2_q11","prompt":"Why are patients encouraged to speak with reception?","options":{"A":"To update insurance information","B":"To report urgent symptoms","C":"To discuss rescheduling options","D":"TO receive medical documents"},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án (C) chính xác: \"To discuss rescheduling options\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."},{"id":"list10_m2_q12","prompt":"What does the announcer imply about today''s appointments?","options":{"A":"Some will be canceled","B":"All patients will still be seen despite delays","C":"Only urgent cases will be seen","D":"Walk-in patients will be prioritized"},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (B): \"All patients will still be seen despite delays\". Đây là suy luận hợp lý nhất từ các chi tiết ngầm định của người nói."}]}},{"id":"list10_m2_t4","title":"Task 4: Academic Lecture 1","task_type":"academic_talk","content":{"context_title":"Bài giảng học thuật 1 (HARD Module)","audio_text":"listen to part of an Agricultural Science class as urban populations continue to grow cities facing pressure to produce more food using limited Land one solution receiving significant attention is vertical farming unlike traditional agriculture vertical farming involves growing crops in stacked involves growing crops in stacked layers inside controlled indoor environments these systems often use artificial lighting automated irrigation and climate control to optimize plant growth one major advantage of vertical farming is efficiency because crops are grown vertically much more food can be produced in a smaller area food can be produced in a smaller area in addition indoor systems reduce exposure to pests decreasing the need for chemical pesticides water usage can also be significantly lower because irrigation systems recycle water instead of allowing it to evaporate or drain away however vertical farming has limit vertical farming has limitations operating these facilities can be expensive due to electricity costs especially for lighting and temperature regulation as a result many vertical Farms focus on high-value crops such as leafy greens rather than grains or fruit trees despite these challenges researchers believe improvements in researchers believe improvements in Energy Efficiency and automation may make vertical farming increasingly practical in the future such systems could help cities improve food security while reducing Transportation costs and environmental impact","questions":[{"id":"list10_m2_q13","prompt":"What is the talk mainly about?","options":{"A":"The environmental problems of traditional farming","B":"The benefits and challenges of vertical farming","C":"The reasons cities are becoming overcrowded","D":"The development of modern irrigation systems"},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án chính xác là (B): \"The benefits and challenges of vertical farming\". Thông tin trọng tâm xuyên suốt bài nghe nhấn mạnh vào ý chính này."},{"id":"list10_m2_q14","prompt":"According to the speaker, why does vertical farming use less water?","options":{"A":"Indoor crops require less irrigation than outdoor crops","B":"Most farms collect and use rainwater","C":"Water is recycled instead of being wasted","D":"Crops grow faster in controlled environments"},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án (C) chính xác: \"Water is recycled instead of being wasted\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."},{"id":"list10_m2_q15","prompt":"Why does the speaker mention leafy greens?","options":{"A":"To give an example of crops that are profitable to grow","B":"To explain which crops need the least water","C":"TO compare indoor farming with outdoor farming","D":"To describe changes in consumer eating habits"},"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Đáp án (A) chính xác: \"To give an example of crops that are profitable to grow\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."},{"id":"list10_m2_q16","prompt":"What does the speaker imply about vertical farming?","options":{"A":"It may soon replace traditional farming completely","B":"Energy costs are still a major challenge","C":"Indoor-grown crops are lower in quality","D":"Most cities already depend on it"},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (B): \"Energy costs are still a major challenge\". Đây là suy luận hợp lý nhất từ các chi tiết ngầm định của người nói."}]}},{"id":"list10_m2_t5","title":"Task 5: Academic Lecture 2","task_type":"academic_talk","content":{"context_title":"Bài giảng học thuật 2 (HARD Module)","audio_text":"listen to part of a macroeconomics class modern economies rely heavily on Global Supply chains which are complex networks linking raw material suppliers manufacturers Transportation infrastructure Distributors and retailers across multiple regions these systems allow these systems allow companies to reduce costs and improve efficiency by sourcing components from wherever production is most economical for instance a single smartphone may contain semiconductors produced in one country Rare Minerals extracted in another and final assembly completed elsewhere this inter elsewhere this interconnected structure offers clear economic advantages but it also creates vulnerability because Supply chains operate as tightly coordinated systems disruption at one point can trigger consequences far beyond the original source of the problem natural disasters labor natural disasters labor shortages Port congestion trade restrictions and geopolitical tensions can all interrupt the movement of goods in some cases even a short-lived disruption at a major shipping hub can cause delays across entire Industries recent Global disruptions have made these Global disruptions have made these weaknesses especially visible delayed shipments can lead to inventory shortages Rising operational costs production slowdowns and declining customer satisfaction in response many firms are reassessing long-standing strategies centered almost exclusively on efficiency what''s exclusively on efficiency this has shifted attention toward resilience the capacity of a system to absorb shocks and recover quickly increasingly experts argue that minimizing costs should no longer be the sole objective future Supply chains may be intentionally less cost efficient in exchange for greater fishing in exchange for greater flexibility redundancy and long-term stability during periods of uncertainty","questions":[{"id":"list10_m2_q17","prompt":"What is the talk mainly about?","options":{"A":"Technological changes in global manufacturing","B":"The benefits and risks of global supply chains","C":"Why smartphone production has become more","D":"The history of international trade"},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án chính xác là (B): \"The benefits and risks of global supply chains\". Thông tin trọng tâm xuyên suốt bài nghe nhấn mạnh vào ý chính này."},{"id":"list10_m2_q18","prompt":"Why does the speaker mention smartphones?","options":{"A":"To show how demand affects production decisions","B":"To compare manufacturing costs across countries","C":"To explain challenges faced by tech companies","D":"To illustrate globally distributed production"},"correct_answer":"D","explanation":"Đáp án (D) chính xác: \"To illustrate globally distributed production\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."},{"id":"list10_m2_q19","prompt":"According to the speaker, what may result from supply chain disruptions?","options":{"A":"Better product quality","B":"Lower transportation costs","C":"Shortages and rising business costs","D":"Faster manufacturing"},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (C): \"Shortages and rising business costs\". Dựa vào chi tiết trực tiếp được người nói đề cập trong bài nghe."},{"id":"list10_m2_q20","prompt":"What does the speaker imply about future supply chains?","options":{"A":"Companies may accept higher costs for greater resilience","B":"Local production will replace global sourcing","C":"Technology will eliminate most supply risks","D":"Efficiency will remain the main priority"},"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (A): \"Companies may accept higher costs for greater resilience\". Đây là suy luận hợp lý nhất từ các chi tiết ngầm định của người nói."}]}}]}],"description":"Bộ đề TOEFL iBT Listening 2026 chuẩn ETS. Chủ đề trọng tâm: Peer review, Chemistry workshop, Supply chain resilience, Ecosystem restoration. Gồm Module 1 (14.5 phút) và Module 2 (14.5 phút - Adaptive) với đầy đủ phản xạ hội thoại, thông báo và bài giảng học thuật.","youtube_url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8blpmDh9i3w","source":"YouTube TOEFL 2026 Listening Practice 10","created_at_ms":1791231607967}'::jsonb,
