  '{"stages":[{"id":"list12_stage_1","title":"Listening - Module 1 (Stage 1)","duration_seconds":870,"description":"Module 1 gồm các dạng bài: Choose a Response, Conversation, Announcement, Academic Talk. Hoàn thành trong 14.5 phút.","tasks":[{"id":"list12_m1_t1","title":"Task 1: Listen & Choose a Response (8 câu)","task_type":"choose_response","content":{"instructions":"Lắng nghe câu nói ngắn và chọn phản xạ trả lời phù hợp nhất theo chuẩn giao tiếp đại học Bắc Mỹ.","questions":[{"id":"list12_m1_q1","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"could you email me the notes later","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"Sure thing.","A":"I wrote everything down.","B":"The email was long.","D":"Notes are helpful."},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (C): \"Sure thing.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list12_m1_q2","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"you were right the answer was saying","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"Multiple choice is tricky.","A":"I knew it!","B":"The test was hard.","D":"I changed my answer."},"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (A): \"I knew it!\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list12_m1_q3","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"I got accepted into graduate school","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"Happy holidays!","A":"Graduate programs are hard.","B":"Congratulations!","D":"Schools are expensive."},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (B): \"Congratulations!\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list12_m1_q4","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"is the lecture hall accessible","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"Accessibility is important.","A":"The hall is big.","B":"I sat in the back.","D":"Yes, there''s an elevator."},"correct_answer":"D","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (D): \"Yes, there''s an elevator.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list12_m1_q5","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"I missed the deadline by one day","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"You should email the instructor.","A":"Deadlines are strict.","B":"One day doesn''t matter.","D":"I missed it too."},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (C): \"You should email the instructor.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list12_m1_q6","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"I got a perfect score on the exam","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"I studied all night.","A":"Scores are posted online.","B":"Get out of here! Seriously?","D":"Exams are stressful."},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (B): \"Get out of here! Seriously?\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list12_m1_q7","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"the instructions mentioned APA style","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"Then you should follow APA format.","A":"Formatting does not make a difference.","B":"I prefer MLA.","D":"Styles are confusing."},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (C): \"Then you should follow APA format.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list12_m1_q8","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"you missed class yesterday everything okay","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"I was feeling under the weather.","A":"Thursdays are always busy.","B":"The lecture was difficult.","D":"Class was canceled."},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (C): \"I was feeling under the weather.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."}]}},{"id":"list12_m1_t2","title":"Task 2: Campus Conversation 1","task_type":"conversation","content":{"context_title":"Hội thoại sinh viên 1","audio_text":"did you hear the library is closing earlier tonight no I didn''t I was planning to stay there until 10:00 because I need to finish my reading assignment they''re shutting down at 7:00 for maintenance the staff needs time to update the computer system and check some equipment I need those books for I need those books for tomorrow''s class and I haven''t finished taking notes yet why don''t you check if the books are available through the online database some of the same materials might be there good idea I''ll look for digital copies when I get home if I can''t find them I''ll come early tomorrow morning good morning","questions":[{"id":"list12_m1_q9","prompt":"Why is the library closing early?","options":{"A":"Because of a holiday","B":"Because of maintenance","C":"Because of a staff meeting","D":"Because of bad weather"},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án (B) chính xác: \"Because of maintenance\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."},{"id":"list12_m1_q10","prompt":"What does the woman decide to do first?","options":{"A":"Finish her assignment at home","B":"Borrow books from a classmate","C":"Look for materials online","D":"Visit the library before seven"},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (C): \"Look for materials online\". Dựa vào chi tiết trực tiếp được người nói đề cập trong bài nghe."}]}},{"id":"list12_m1_t3","title":"Task 3: Campus Conversation 2","task_type":"conversation","content":{"context_title":"Hội thoại sinh viên 2","audio_text":"the microscope images look much blurrier than yesterday I see did you change any of the settings or use a different sample know I used the same settings as before but the equipment be the problem after yesterday''s maintenance can someone adjust it this afternoon I need to continue my experiments soon and make the necessary adjustments that''s great I''ll return after my chemistry seminar and see if the images improve","questions":[{"id":"list12_m1_q11","prompt":"Why does the student speak with the staff member?","options":{"A":"To request permission to use another laboratory.","B":"To report a problem with the microscope.","C":"TO reserve the laboratory technician for tomorrow.","D":"To borrow additional sample slides."},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án (B) chính xác: \"To report a problem with the microscope.\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."},{"id":"list12_m1_q12","prompt":"What will the student most likely do next?","options":{"A":"Attend a chemistry seminar before returning","B":"Replace the microscope with another model.","C":"Clean every microscope in the laboratory.","D":"Submit the blurred images to the instructor."},"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (A): \"Attend a chemistry seminar before returning\". Dựa vào chi tiết trực tiếp được người nói đề cập trong bài nghe."}]}},{"id":"list12_m1_t4","title":"Task 4: Campus Announcement 1","task_type":"announcement","content":{"context_title":"Thông báo khuôn viên trường 1","audio_text":"listen to an announcement on campus the campus printing center will be unavailable this Friday morning while new printers are installed students who need to print documents before noon should use the machines in the library or Student Union existing printing balances will remain active and no additional charges will be applied during the additional charges will be applied during the maintenance period the center is expected to reopen at 1 p.m.","questions":[{"id":"list12_m1_q13","prompt":"Why will the printing center be unavailable?","options":{"A":"Staff members are receiving training.","B":"New equipment is being installed.","C":"The building requires repairs.","D":"Student accounts are being updated."},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án (B) chính xác: \"New equipment is being installed.\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."},{"id":"list12_m1_q14","prompt":"What should students do if they need to print documents?","options":{"A":"Wait until the following day.","B":"Purchase a new printing card.","C":"Use another campus location.","D":"Contact the printing center staff."},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (C): \"Use another campus location.\". Dựa vào chi tiết trực tiếp được người nói đề cập trong bài nghe."}]}},{"id":"list12_m1_t5","title":"Task 5: Campus Announcement 2","task_type":"announcement","content":{"context_title":"Thông báo khuôn viên trường 2","audio_text":"listen to an announcement in a lecture hall the history department is changing the location of Friday''s guest lecture the event will now take place in arts hall 201 instead of the main Auditorium because of a scheduling conflict the starting time remains 5:00 p.m. and students who already registered can students who already registered do not need to sign up again additional seats will be available on a first-come first-served basis","questions":[{"id":"list12_m1_q15","prompt":"Why was the lecture location changed?","options":{"A":"The speaker requested a smaller room.","B":"The auditorium is being renovated.","C":"Another event created a scheduling conflict.","D":"Too few students registered."},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án (C) chính xác: \"Another event created a scheduling conflict.\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."},{"id":"list12_m1_q16","prompt":"What do registered students need to do?","options":{"A":"Register again online.","B":"Arrive at the new location.","C":"Contact the department office.","D":"Attend the lecture at a different time."},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (B): \"Arrive at the new location.\". Dựa vào chi tiết trực tiếp được người nói đề cập trong bài nghe."}]}},{"id":"list12_m1_t6","title":"Task 6: Academic Lecture","task_type":"academic_talk","content":{"context_title":"Bài giảng học thuật đại học","audio_text":"listen to part of an environmental science class artificial light has transformed Modern Life by making nighttime activities safer and more convenient however excessive artificial lighting can create a problem known as light pollution this occurs when unnecessary or poorly directed changes natural patterns of Darkness one major effect of light pollution is that it makes astronomical observation more difficult bright Skies caused by artificial light can hide faint stars and other celestial objects light pollution can also affect Wildlife because many depend on natural cycles of light and darkness for activities such as navigation feeding and reproduction to reduce these effects some communities are introducing dark sky measures these include using shielded lights reducing unnecessary illumination and choosing minimize environmental disruption although some people worry that reducing night time lighting could create safety problems experts argue that carefully Design Systems can provide both visibility and conservation benefits module 2","questions":[{"id":"list12_m1_q17","prompt":"What is the talk mainly about?","options":{"A":"The history of artificial lighting technology","B":"The effects of light pollution and ways to reduce it","C":"The methods scientists use to study wildlife","D":"The importance of observing stars and planets"},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án chính xác là (B): \"The effects of light pollution and ways to reduce it\". Thông tin trọng tâm xuyên suốt bài nghe nhấn mạnh vào ý chính này."},{"id":"list12_m1_q18","prompt":"According to the speaker, why does light pollution affect astronomical observation?","options":{"A":"It changes the movement of stars and planets.","B":"It makes faint objects in the sky harder to see.","C":"It damages scientific equipment used by astronomers.","D":"It prevents researchers from studying weather patterns."},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án (B) chính xác: \"It makes faint objects in the sky harder to see.\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."},{"id":"list12_m1_q19","prompt":"Why does the speaker mention wildlife?","options":{"A":"To explain another area affected by excessive artificial light","B":"To show that animals benefit from brighter environments","C":"To describe how scientists classify different species","D":"To compare wildlife research with astronomy"},"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Đáp án (A) chính xác: \"To explain another area affected by excessive artificial light\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."},{"id":"list12_m1_q20","prompt":"What does the speaker imply about communities that adopt dark sky measures?","options":{"A":"They usually spend more money than communities with","B":"They must completely eliminate artificial lighting at night.","C":"They are mainly interested in helping astronomers study the","D":"They may reduce environmental impacts while still meeting"},"correct_answer":"D","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (D): \"They may reduce environmental impacts while still meeting\". Đây là suy luận hợp lý nhất từ các chi tiết ngầm định của người nói."}]}}]},{"id":"list12_stage_2","title":"Listening - Module 2 (Stage 2 - HARD)","duration_seconds":870,"description":"Module 2 cấp độ nâng cao (Hard): kiểm tra khả năng suy luận, nắm bắt ý chính và chi tiết học thuật.","tasks":[{"id":"list12_m2_t1","title":"Task 1: Listen & Choose a Response (8 câu)","task_type":"choose_response","content":{"instructions":"Lắng nghe câu nói ngắn và chọn phản xạ trả lời phù hợp nhất theo chuẩn giao tiếp đại học Bắc Mỹ.","questions":[{"id":"list12_m2_q1","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"could you print these slides before class","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"I''ll send them to the printer right away.","A":"The printer uses recycled paper.","B":"The slides include several diagrams.","D":"Our class starts at nine."},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (C): \"I''ll send them to the printer right away.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list12_m2_q2","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"I can''t remember my locker combination","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"The lockers were installed last semester.","A":"The hallway gets crowded before lunch.","B":"My backpack is still inside the locker.","D":"You can ask the front office to look it up."},"correct_answer":"D","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (D): \"You can ask the front office to look it up.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list12_m2_q3","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"have you seen my calculator anywhere","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"I borrowed a ruler from the library.","A":"The calculator has fresh batteries.","B":"Tomorrow''s quiz covers statistics.","D":"It might still be on the table in the"},"correct_answer":"D","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (D): \"It might still be on the table in the\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list12_m2_q4","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"I''m running a little late for the meeting","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"Several new employees joined this week.","A":"I''ll save you a seat near the front.","B":"The meeting agenda was emailed yesterday.","D":"The conference room overlooks the"},"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (A): \"I''ll save you a seat near the front.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list12_m2_q5","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"do you know when the bookstore opens","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"The bookstore sells used textbooks.","A":"My history book was expensive.","B":"Students often study in the café nearby.","D":"It usually opens at eight on weekdays."},"correct_answer":"D","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (D): \"It usually opens at eight on weekdays.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list12_m2_q6","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"I think I left my water bottle in the lecture hall","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"The lecture hall has comfortable seats.","A":"The lecture lasted almost two hours.","B":"You should check the lost-and-found office.","D":"The bottle is made of stainless steel."},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (B): \"You should check the lost-and-found office.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list12_m2_q7","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"can you help me move these boxes","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"The boxes contain old project files.","A":"The storage room is on the second floor.","B":"We finished organizing the shelves yesterday.","D":"Sure, where would you like me to take them?"},"correct_answer":"D","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (D): \"Sure, where would you like me to take them?\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."},{"id":"list12_m2_q8","type":"choose_response","audio_text":"I haven''t received the assignment instructions yet","prompt":"Select the most appropriate response to what you heard:","options":{"C":"The deadline is next Friday.","A":"The professor usually posts them on the course website.","B":"Several students asked questions after class.","D":"The assignment is worth twenty percent Of the final"},"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (A): \"The professor usually posts them on the course website.\". Đây là câu phản xạ giao tiếp tự nhiên và chuẩn xác nhất theo ngữ cảnh văn hóa đại học Bắc Mỹ."}]}},{"id":"list12_m2_t2","title":"Task 2: Campus Conversation","task_type":"conversation","content":{"context_title":"Hội thoại sinh viên (Phần nâng cao)","audio_text":"my presentation file won''t open on the classroom computer that''s strange did you check whether the file was damaged I opened it successfully on my laptop so I think the problem is with the classroom computer still has the previous version of the software installed so it may not support some of the is there a quick solution I have to present in less than an hour yes open the file on another computer and save it as a PDF that should prevent compatibility issues and preserve the formatting that makes sense I''ll use the library computers before I''ll use the library computers before class and create a new copy their good just make sure you test the PDF before your presentation starts","questions":[{"id":"list12_m2_q9","prompt":"Why is the student having a problem?","options":{"A":"The presentation was deleted.","B":"The classroom computer has older software.","C":"The library computers are unavailable.","D":"The classroom projector is broken."},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án (B) chính xác: \"The classroom computer has older software.\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."},{"id":"list12_m2_q10","prompt":"What will the student most likely do?","options":{"A":"Cancel the presentation.","B":"Install new software in the classroom.","C":"Save the presentation as a PDE","D":"Print paper copies instead."},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (C): \"Save the presentation as a PDE\". Dựa vào chi tiết trực tiếp được người nói đề cập trong bài nghe."}]}},{"id":"list12_m2_t3","title":"Task 3: Campus Announcement","task_type":"announcement","content":{"context_title":"Thông báo khuôn viên trường (Phần nâng cao)","audio_text":"listen to an announcement on campus the chemistry department has extended the deadline for laboratory reports by 2 days due to a problem with the online submission system students who already submitted their reports do not need to upload them again however anyone who experienced technical difficulty should complete the submission before they should complete the submission before midnight on the new deadline the department apologizes for the inconvenience","questions":[{"id":"list12_m2_q11","prompt":"Why was the deadline extended?","options":{"A":"Students requested more preparation time.","B":"The laboratory schedule changed.","C":"The submission system had problems.","D":"The instructor was unavailable."},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án (C) chính xác: \"The submission system had problems.\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."},{"id":"list12_m2_q12","prompt":"What should students who already submitted reports do?","options":{"A":"Upload their reports again.","B":"Contact the department immediately.","C":"Make changes before the deadline.","D":"Take no further action."},"correct_answer":"D","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (D): \"Take no further action.\". Dựa vào chi tiết trực tiếp được người nói đề cập trong bài nghe."}]}},{"id":"list12_m2_t4","title":"Task 4: Academic Lecture 1","task_type":"academic_talk","content":{"context_title":"Bài giảng học thuật 1 (HARD Module)","audio_text":"listen to part of a business administration class many companies are increasingly adopting subscription-based business models in which customers make regular payments to access products or Services rather than purchasing them permanently this approach has expanded Beyond traditional areas such as magazines and memberships and is now common in software entertainment and other Industries for businesses subscriptions provide a more stable source of Revenue making it easier to plan Investments and predict future earnings they also encourage companies to focus on maintaining customer satisfaction because long-term success depends on retaining subscribers friends on retaining subscribers however this model can create challenges for consumers because payments are often small and recurring people may lose track of their total spending or continue paying for services they no longer use a subscription models continue to grow experts argue that companies will need to prioritize companies will need to prioritize transparency and demonstrate clear value to maintain consumer Trust","questions":[{"id":"list12_m2_q13","prompt":"What is the talk mainly about?","options":{"A":"The history Of product ownership in modern economies","B":"The expansion of subscription models and their effects on","C":"The role of technology in reducing business expenses","D":"The reasons companies use advertising to attract new"},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án chính xác là (B): \"The expansion of subscription models and their effects on\". Thông tin trọng tâm xuyên suốt bài nghe nhấn mạnh vào ý chính này."},{"id":"list12_m2_q14","prompt":"According to the speaker, why do businesses benefit from subscription models?","options":{"A":"They no longer need to improve their products or services.","B":"They can avoid competition from Other companies.","C":"They can predict revenue more easily and plan future decisions.","D":"They can prevent customers from canceling services."},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án (C) chính xác: \"They can predict revenue more easily and plan future decisions.\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."},{"id":"list12_m2_q15","prompt":"Why does the speaker mention consumers continuing to pay for unused services?","options":{"A":"To illustrate a potential problem caused by recurring payments.","B":"To describe how companies attract new subscribers.","C":"To explain why customers prefer buying products permanently.","D":"To show that most subscription services are unsuccessful."},"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Đáp án (A) chính xác: \"To illustrate a potential problem caused by recurring payments.\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."},{"id":"list12_m2_q16","prompt":"What does the speaker imply about the future of subscription-based businesses?","options":{"A":"Businesses will no longer depend on customer satisfaction.","B":"Consumers will eventually stop using subscription services.","C":"Companies will need to provide clear value and maintain","D":"Subscription models will replace all traditional purchasing"},"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (C): \"Companies will need to provide clear value and maintain\". Đây là suy luận hợp lý nhất từ các chi tiết ngầm định của người nói."}]}},{"id":"list12_m2_t5","title":"Task 5: Academic Lecture 2","task_type":"academic_talk","content":{"context_title":"Bài giảng học thuật 2 (HARD Module)","audio_text":"listen to part of a public health class noise pollution refers to excessive or unwanted sound that interferes with human activities and well-being although it is often considered less serious than other forms of pollution researchers have found that prolonged exposure to high noise levels can have significant consequences levels can have significant consequences in urban environments major sources include Transportation Systems Construction industrial operations and densely populated areas studies indicate that continuous exposure to excessive noise can contribute to increased stress sleep disruption and sleep disruption and reduced ability to concentrate overtime it may also be associated with health concerns including cardiovascular conditions such as elevated blood pressure to address these problems cities have introduced various strategies including redesigning Urban spaces redesigning Urban spaces limiting construction hours and installing barriers that block or absorb sound however experts emphasized that the goal is not to eliminate all noise which would be unrealistic in active communities instead effective sound management aims to create healthier environments while all healthier environments while allowing cities to continue functioning","questions":[{"id":"list12_m2_q17","prompt":"What is the talk mainly about?","options":{"A":"The ways cities are expanding transportation and","B":"The causes of noise pollution, its effects on health, and","C":"The differences between natural and human-made sounds","D":"The reasons urban environments are becoming"},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án chính xác là (B): \"The causes of noise pollution, its effects on health, and\". Thông tin trọng tâm xuyên suốt bài nghe nhấn mạnh vào ý chính này."},{"id":"list12_m2_q18","prompt":"According to the speaker, what health consequence may result from long-term exposure to excessive noise?","options":{"A":"A higher risk Of cardiovascular problems such as high blood","B":"A greater likelihood of developing allergies caused by","C":"A permanent loss of concentration during daily activities","D":"A decrease in physical activity caused by urban conditions"},"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (A): \"A higher risk Of cardiovascular problems such as high blood\". Dựa vào chi tiết trực tiếp được người nói đề cập trong bài nghe."},{"id":"list12_m2_q19","prompt":"Why does the speaker mention sound barriers?","options":{"A":"To explain one example of a strategy used to reduce","B":"To show why highway construction creates unavoidable","C":"To compare different materials used in modern buildings","D":"To describe why cities spend more money on"},"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Đáp án (A) chính xác: \"To explain one example of a strategy used to reduce\". Người nói đã giải thích rõ lý do này trong đoạn ghi âm."},{"id":"list12_m2_q20","prompt":"What does the speaker imply about managing noise pollution in cities?","options":{"A":"Urban areas should eliminate most sources of sound to protect residents.","B":"Complete silence is unnecessary because cities need to remain","C":"Noise pollution is mainly a temporary problem caused by construction.","D":"Most cities have already solved the problem through improved planning."},"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Đáp án đúng là (B): \"Complete silence is unnecessary because cities need to remain\". Đây là suy luận hợp lý nhất từ các chi tiết ngầm định của người nói."}]}}]}],"description":"Bộ đề TOEFL iBT Listening 2026 chuẩn ETS. Chủ đề trọng tâm: Professor consultation, Campus recycling program, Urban noise pollution, Marine biology. Gồm Module 1 (14.5 phút) và Module 2 (14.5 phút - Adaptive) với đầy đủ phản xạ hội thoại, thông báo và bài giảng học thuật.","youtube_url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eIghx_j95k4","source":"YouTube TOEFL 2026 Listening Practice 12","created_at_ms":1791231607970}'::jsonb,
  timezone('utc'::text, now())
)
